From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roshan Gautam <roshangautam07@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:04:04 +0545
Subject: [PATCH 01/74] build: fix compilation with Apple clang 21

Building the unmodified v18.20.8 tree with Xcode 26 (Apple clang 21,
macOS 26 SDK) fails in V8's bundled zlib (target v8_zlib):

  deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h:151:33: note: expanded from macro
      'fdopen'
  #  define fdopen(fd,mode) NULL /* No fdopen() */
  MacOSX.sdk/usr/include/_stdio.h:322:7: error: expected identifier
      or '('
  FILE *fdopen(int, const char *) __DARWIN_ALIAS_STARTING(...);

zutil.h treats any target that defines TARGET_OS_MAC as classic Mac OS
and defines fdopen() away as a macro. With the newer SDK,
TargetConditionals.h (which defines TARGET_OS_MAC) is already visible
when zutil.h is processed, and zutil.c includes zutil.h before gzguts.h
pulls in <stdio.h>, so the SDK's fdopen() declaration is macro-expanded
into invalid code.

Apply the same fix upstream zlib made (and that Node.js' own deps/zlib
already carries): only key the classic Mac OS block off MACOS, not
TARGET_OS_MAC. macOS builds still get OS_CODE 19 from the existing
__APPLE__ block further down, so the only behavioural change is that
the real fdopen() is used. Only the copy under deps/v8 is affected;
deps/zlib already has this change.

No other source changes were needed for the unpatched v18.20.8 tree to
build with this toolchain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h b/deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h
index ec1993f3f7..b8337eb70e 100644
--- a/deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h
+++ b/deps/v8/third_party/zlib/zutil.h
@@ -141,7 +141,7 @@ extern z_const char * const z_errmsg[10]; /* indexed by 2-zlib_error */
 #  endif
 #endif
 
-#if defined(MACOS) || defined(TARGET_OS_MAC)
+#if defined(MACOS)
 #  define OS_CODE  7
 #  ifndef Z_SOLO
 #    if defined(__MWERKS__) && __dest_os != __be_os && __dest_os != __win32_os
